--
N5008 [namespace.memdef]/3 + [temp.friend]/1: a friend function
template declared with a QUALIFIED name (`friend int det::algo(...)`)
refers to the template previously declared in that namespace and
introduces no new name; the referred-to template is a friend, so its
body may bind a reference to the class's PRIVATE base.  libstdc++'s
match_results (privately derived from vector<sub_match>) befriends
`__detail::__regex_algo_impl`, whose `_Unchecked& __res = __m` failed
"bad reference initializer" and left every std::regex_match a havoc
stub.  The unqualified friend path looked the name up in the innermost
enclosing namespace and recorded nothing.
